    },
    "q-73478": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73478",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
